{"id":"mahabharata-5-141","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":141,"title":"एकचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 141 · Karna's dream of doom","summary":{"en":"Karna tells Krishna of the dreadful omens he has seen and a dream in which Yudhishthira and his brothers ascended a white palace and feasted, while Duryodhana and his allies went south towards death. They embrace, and Krishna drives on with Satyaki.","kn":"ತಾನು ಕಂಡ ಭೀಕರ ಶಕುನಗಳನ್ನೂ, ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಮತ್ತು ಸಹೋದರರು ಶ್ವೇತಪ್ರಾಸಾದವೇರಿ ಔತಣ ಮಾಡಿದ, ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಮತ್ತು ಮಿತ್ರರು ದಕ್ಷಿಣದತ್ತ ಮೃತ್ಯುವಿಗೆ ಹೋದ ಕನಸನ್ನೂ ಕರ್ಣನು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಅಪ್ಪಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮುಂದೆ ಸಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कर्ण श्रीकृष्ण को देखे गए भयानक अपशकुन और एक स्वप्न बताता है जिसमें युधिष्ठिर और उनके भाई एक श्वेत महल पर चढ़कर भोज कर रहे थे, जबकि दुर्योधन और उसके मित्र दक्षिण की ओर मृत्यु की ओर जा रहे थे। दोनों गले मिलते हैं, और श्रीकृष्ण सात्यकि के साथ आगे बढ़ जाते हैं।","te":"తాను చూసిన భయంకర శకునాలను, యుధిష్ఠిరుడు, సోదరులు తెల్లని ప్రాసాదం ఎక్కి విందు చేస్తుండగా దుర్యోధనుడు, మిత్రులు దక్షిణం వైపు మృత్యువుకు వెళ్తున్న కలను కర్ణుడు శ్రీకృష్ణునికి చెబుతాడు. ఇద్దరూ కౌగిలించుకుంటారు, శ్రీకృష్ణుడు సాత్యకితో ముందుకు సాగుతాడు.","ta":"தான் கண்ட கொடிய சகுனங்களையும், யுதிஷ்டிரரும் சகோதரர்களும் வெண்மாளிகையில் ஏறி விருந்துண்ண, துரியோதனனும் நண்பர்களும் தெற்கு நோக்கி மரணத்துக்குச் சென்ற கனவையும் கர்ணன் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரிடம் சொல்கிறான். இருவரும் தழுவிக்கொள்ள, ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் ஸாத்யகியுடன் தொடர்ந்து செல்கிறார்.","ml":"താൻ കണ്ട ഭയങ്കരമായ ദുർലക്ഷണങ്ങളും, യുധിഷ്ഠിരനും സഹോദരന്മാരും വെളുത്ത കൊട്ടാരത്തിൽ കയറി വിരുന്നുണ്ണുന്നതും, ദുര്യോധനനും സഖ്യകക്ഷികളും മരണത്തിലേക്ക് തെക്കോട്ട് പോകുന്നതുമായ സ്വപ്നവും കർണ്ണൻ കൃഷ്ണനോട് പറയുന്നു. അവർ പരസ്പരം ആലിംഗനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; സാത്യകിയോടൊപ്പം കൃഷ്ണൻ തേരോടിച്ചുപോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.141; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"कर्णोपनिवादपर्व","titleEn":"Karnopanivada Parva (The secret talks with Karna)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"केशवस्य तु तद्वाक्यं कर्णः श्रुत्वा हितं शुभम् ।\nअब्रवीदभिसंपूज्य कृष्णं मधुनिषूदनम् ।\nजानन्मां किं महाबाहो संमोहयितुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Keshava's good and beneficial words, Karna honored Krishna, slayer of Madhu, and said: \"Mighty-armed one, you know all this; why do you want to bewilder me?"}},{"n":2,"text":"योऽयं पृथिव्याः कार्त्स्न्येन विनाशः समुपस्थितः ।\nनिमित्तं तत्र शकुनिरहं दुःशासनस्तथा ।\nदुर्योधनश्च नृपतिर्धृतराष्ट्रसुतोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The total destruction of the earth that has now come about has as its causes Shakuni, myself, Duhshasana, and King Duryodhana, son of Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":3,"text":"असंशयमिदं कृष्ण महद्युद्धमुपस्थितम् ।\nपाण्डवानां कुरूणां च घोरं रुधिरकर्दमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without doubt, Krishna, a great and terrible war, with mud of blood, has come between the Pandavas and the Kurus."}},{"n":4,"text":"राजानो राजपुत्राश्च दुर्योधनवशानुगाः ।\nरणे शस्त्राग्निना दग्धाः प्राप्स्यन्ति यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings and princes who follow Duryodhana's will, burned in battle by the fire of weapons, will go to Yama's abode."}},{"n":5,"text":"स्वप्ना हि बहवो घोरा दृश्यन्ते मधुसूदन ।\nनिमित्तानि च घोराणि तथोत्पाताः सुदारुणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, many dreadful dreams are seen, and fearful omens and very harsh portents,"}},{"n":6,"text":"पराजयं धार्तराष्ट्रे विजयं च युधिष्ठिरे ।\nशंसन्त इव वार्ष्णेय विविधा लोमहर्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"of many hair-raising kinds, as if proclaiming defeat for Dhritarashtra's son and victory for Yudhishthira, Vrishni hero."}},{"n":7,"text":"प्राजापत्यं हि नक्षत्रं ग्रहस्तीक्ष्णो महाद्युतिः ।\nशनैश्चरः पीडयति पीडयन्प्राणिनोऽधिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fierce, brilliant planet Saturn oppresses the Prajapati star and torments beings all the more."}},{"n":8,"text":"कृत्वा चाङ्गारको वक्रं ज्येष्ठायां मधुसूदन ।\nअनुराधां प्रार्थयते मैत्रं संशमयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mars, Madhusudana, having turned in retrograde in Jyeshtha, seeks Anuradha, as if bringing the friend-star to harm."}},{"n":9,"text":"नूनं महद्भयं कृष्ण कुरूणां समुपस्थितम् ।\nविशेषेण हि वार्ष्णेय चित्रां पीडयते ग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, surely a great fear has come for the Kurus; especially, Vrishni hero, a planet afflicts Chitra."}},{"n":10,"text":"सोमस्य लक्ष्म व्यावृत्तं राहुरर्कमुपेष्यति ।\nदिवश्चोल्काः पतन्त्येताः सनिर्घाताः सकम्पनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mark on the moon has turned, and Rahu will approach the sun. These meteors fall from the sky with thunderclaps and tremors."}},{"n":11,"text":"निष्टनन्ति च मातङ्गा मुञ्चन्त्यश्रूणि वाजिनः ।\nपानीयं यवसं चापि नाभिनन्दन्ति माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants groan and horses shed tears; they take no pleasure in water or fodder, Madhava."}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रादुर्भूतेषु चैतेषु भयमाहुरुपस्थितम् ।\nनिमित्तेषु महाबाहो दारुणं प्राणिनाशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say that when such omens appear, a dreadful fear that destroys life has come, mighty-armed one."}},{"n":13,"text":"अल्पे भुक्ते पुरीषं च प्रभूतमिह दृश्यते ।\nवाजिनां वारणानां च मनुष्याणां च केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Keshava, little is eaten, yet much dung is seen among horses, elephants and men,"}},{"n":14,"text":"धार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैन्येषु सर्वेषु मधुसूदन ।\nपराभवस्य तल्लिङ्गमिति प्राहुर्मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"in all the armies of Dhritarashtra's son, Madhusudana. The wise call this a sign of defeat."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रहृष्टं वाहनं कृष्ण पाण्डवानां प्रचक्षते ।\nप्रदक्षिणा मृगाश्चैव तत्तेषां जयलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say the mounts of the Pandavas are cheerful, Krishna, and the animals keep to their right; this is a sign of their victory."}},{"n":16,"text":"अपसव्या मृगाः सर्वे धार्तराष्ट्रस्य केशव ।\nवाचश्चाप्यशरीरिण्यस्तत्पराभवलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the animals of Dhritarashtra's son turn to the left, Keshava, and bodiless voices speak; this is a sign of his defeat."}},{"n":17,"text":"मयूराः पुष्पशकुना हंसाः सारसचातकाः ।\nजीवं जीवकसंघाश्चाप्यनुगच्छन्ति पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Peacocks, flower-birds, swans, cranes and chataka birds, and flocks of jivajivaka partridges follow the Pandavas."}},{"n":18,"text":"गृध्राः काका बडाः श्येना यातुधानाः शलावृकाः ।\nमक्षिकाणां च संघाता अनुगच्छन्ति कौरवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vultures, crows, herons, hawks, rakshasas, jackals and swarms of flies follow the Kauravas."}},{"n":19,"text":"धार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैन्येषु भेरीणां नास्ति निस्वनः ।\nअनाहताः पाण्डवानां नदन्ति पटहाः किल ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the armies of Dhritarashtra's son no kettledrum sounds, while the Pandavas' drums are said to roar though unstruck."}},{"n":20,"text":"उदपानाश्च नर्दन्ति यथा गोवृषभास्तथा ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैन्येषु तत्पराभवलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wells bellow like cows and bulls in the armies of Dhritarashtra's son; that is a sign of defeat."}},{"n":21,"text":"मांसशोणितवर्षं च वृष्टं देवेन माधव ।\nतथा गन्धर्वनगरं भानुमन्तमुपस्थितम् ।\nसप्राकारं सपरिखं सवप्रं चारुतोरणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhava, the sky rained flesh and blood, and a city of the gandharvas, shining like the sun, appeared, with ramparts, moat, embankment and lovely gateways."}},{"n":22,"text":"कृष्णश्च परिघस्तत्र भानुमावृत्य तिष्ठति ।\nउदयास्तमये संध्ये वेदयानो महद्भयम् ।\nएका सृग्वाशते घोरं तत्पराभवलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A dark bar stands covering the sun at its rising and setting, and at dawn and dusk a single jackal howls horribly, announcing great fear; this is a sign of defeat."}},{"n":23,"text":"कृष्णग्रीवाश्च शकुना लम्बमाना भयानकाः ।\nसंध्यामभिमुखा यान्ति तत्पराभवलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Black-necked birds, hanging in the air and fearsome, fly toward the twilight; this is a sign of defeat."}},{"n":24,"text":"ब्राह्मणान्प्रथमं द्वेष्टि गुरूंश्च मधुसूदन ।\nभृत्यान्भक्तिमतश्चापि तत्पराभवलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, he first hates brahmins and elders, and even devoted servants; this is a sign of defeat."}},{"n":25,"text":"पूर्वा दिग्लोहिताकारा शस्त्रवर्णा च दक्षिणा ।\nआमपात्रप्रतीकाशा पश्चिमा मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The east is the color of blood, the south the color of weapons, and the west, Madhusudana, is like an unbaked clay pot."}},{"n":26,"text":"प्रदीप्ताश्च दिशः सर्वा धार्तराष्ट्रस्य माधव ।\nमहद्भयं वेदयन्ति तस्मिन्नुत्पातलक्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the quarters around Dhritarashtra's son are ablaze, Madhava, announcing a great danger in this display of portents."}},{"n":27,"text":"सहस्रपादं प्रासादं स्वप्नान्ते स्म युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअधिरोहन्मया दृष्टः सह भ्रातृभिरच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Achyuta, at the end of a dream I saw Yudhishthira climb a palace of a thousand pillars with his brothers."}},{"n":28,"text":"श्वेतोष्णीषाश्च दृश्यन्ते सर्वे ते शुक्लवाससः ।\nआसनानि च शुभ्राणि सर्वेषामुपलक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"They all appear in white turbans and white clothes, and I notice bright seats for all of them."}},{"n":29,"text":"तव चापि मया कृष्ण स्वप्नान्ते रुधिराविला ।\nआन्त्रेण पृथिवी दृष्टा परिक्षिप्ता जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"And in a dream, Krishna, I saw the earth, Janardana, muddied with blood and encircled by entrails."}},{"n":30,"text":"अस्थिसंचयमारूढश्चामितौजा युधिष्ठिरः ।\nसुवर्णपात्र्यां संहृष्टो भुक्तवान्घृतपायसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I saw immeasurably mighty Yudhishthira, standing on a heap of bones, joyfully eating ghee and milk-rice from a golden dish."}},{"n":31,"text":"युधिष्ठिरो मया दृष्टो ग्रसमानो वसुंधराम् ।\nत्वया दत्तामिमां व्यक्तं भोक्ष्यते स वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I saw Yudhishthira swallowing the earth; clearly he will enjoy this earth you have given him."}},{"n":32,"text":"उच्चं पर्वतमारूढो भीमकर्मा वृकोदरः ।\nगदापाणिर्नरव्याघ्रो वीक्षन्निव महीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I saw Vrikodara, of terrible deeds, climbing a high mountain, mace in hand, that tiger among men looking over this earth."}},{"n":33,"text":"क्षपयिष्यति नः सर्वान्स सुव्यक्तं महारणे ।\nविदितं मे हृषीकेश यतो धर्मस्ततो जयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He will surely destroy us all in the great battle. I know it, Hrishikesha: where dharma is, there is victory."}},{"n":34,"text":"पाण्डुरं गजमारूढो गाण्डीवी स धनंजयः ।\nत्वया सार्धं हृषीकेश श्रिया परमया ज्वलन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I saw Gandiva's bearer Dhananjaya mounted on a white elephant, blazing with supreme splendor, together with you, Hrishikesha."}},{"n":35,"text":"यूयं सर्वान्वधिष्यध्वं तत्र मे नास्ति संशयः ।\nपार्थिवान्समरे कृष्ण दुर्योधनपुरोगमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will kill all the kings in battle, with Duryodhana at their head; in this I have no doubt, Krishna."}},{"n":36,"text":"नकुलः सहदेवश्च सात्यकिश्च महारथः ।\nशुद्धकेयूरकण्ठत्राः शुक्लमाल्याम्बरावृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, Sahadeva and the great chariot-warrior Satyaki, with spotless armlets and necklaces, wearing white garlands and clothes,"}},{"n":37,"text":"अधिरूढा नरव्याघ्रा नरवाहनमुत्तमम् ।\nत्रय एते महामात्राः पाण्डुरच्छत्रवाससः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those tigers among men, mounted on the best of vehicles carried by men, and these three great ministers wearing white umbrellas and garments,"}},{"n":38,"text":"श्वेतोष्णीषाश्च दृश्यन्ते त्रय एव जनार्दन ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रस्य सैन्येषु तान्विजानीहि केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"are seen in white turbans, only three, Janardana. Know them in the armies of Dhritarashtra's son, Keshava."}},{"n":39,"text":"अश्वत्थामा कृपश्चैव कृतवर्मा च सात्वतः ।\nरक्तोष्णीषाश्च दृश्यन्ते सर्वे माधव पार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthama, Kripa, and Kritavarman of the Satvatas are seen with red turbans, Madhava, as are all the kings."}},{"n":40,"text":"उष्ट्रयुक्तं समारूढौ भीष्मद्रोणौ जनार्दन ।\nमया सार्धं महाबाहो धार्तराष्ट्रेण चाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma and Drona, Janardana, mounted a camel-drawn cart with me and Dhritarashtra's son, mighty one."}},{"n":41,"text":"अगस्त्यशास्तां च दिशं प्रयाताः स्म जनार्दन ।\nअचिरेणैव कालेन प्राप्स्यामो यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana, we were going toward the quarter ruled by Agastya. Soon we shall reach Yama's abode."}},{"n":42,"text":"अहं चान्ये च राजानो यच्च तत्क्षत्रमण्डलम् ।\nगाण्डीवाग्निं प्रवेक्ष्याम इति मे नास्ति संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I, the other kings and that whole circle of kshatriyas will enter the fire of Gandiva; of that I have no doubt.\""}},{"text":"कृष्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Krishna said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"उपस्थितविनाशेयं नूनमद्य वसुंधरा ।\nतथा हि मे वचः कर्ण नोपैति हृदयं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely this earth is now facing destruction, Karna, since my words do not reach your heart."}},{"n":44,"text":"सर्वेषां तात भूतानां विनाशे समुपस्थिते ।\nअनयो नयसंकाशो हृदयान्नापसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My friend, when the destruction of all beings is at hand, wrong that looks like right does not leave the heart."}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":45,"text":"अपि त्वा कृष्ण पश्याम जीवन्तोऽस्मान्महारणात् ।\nसमुत्तीर्णा महाबाहो वीरक्षयविनाशनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, if we see you again, having come alive through the great battle, the destroyer of heroes,"}},{"n":46,"text":"अथ वा संगमः कृष्ण स्वर्गे नो भविता ध्रुवम् ।\nतत्रेदानीं समेष्यामः पुनः सार्धं त्वयानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"or else, Krishna, we shall surely meet in heaven. Then we shall meet again there with you, blameless one."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":47,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा माधवं कर्णः परिष्वज्य च पीडितम् ।\nविसर्जितः केशवेन रथोपस्थादवातरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Karna embraced the grieved Madhava, and, dismissed by Keshava, got down from the chariot's seat."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततः स्वरथमास्थाय जाम्बूनदविभूषितम् ।\nसहास्माभिर्निववृते राधेयो दीनमानसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he mounted his own gold-adorned chariot and returned with us, Radha's son, with a sad heart."}},{"n":49,"text":"ततः शीघ्रतरं प्रायात्केशवः सहसात्यकिः ।\nपुनरुच्चारयन्वाणीं याहि याहीति सारथिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Keshava, with Satyaki, went on more swiftly, repeatedly saying to the charioteer, \"Go, go!\""}}]}]}